[N 25-26 Blackfathom Deeps]
[D Forever Druid 1-30 (Braedyn)\\The Blackfathom Deeps run from the Zoram Strand as cat damage behind a tank: Researching the Corruption, Twilight Falls, In Search of Thaelrid and Blackfathom Villainy, with boss notes, loot calls and the hearth home.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 25|r  -  you stand on the Zoram Strand in north-west Ashenvale; hearth = Sentinel Hill. This chapter is one dungeon, Blackfathom Deeps: a full clear of 22-28 mobs with bosses at 25-28. Only Thaelrid pays out inside (2,400 XP); the other quests are finished here and handed in later: about 10,650 quest XP in all. Group content: bring a tank and a healer; you are cat damage
[OC]|cffffcc00Log check:|r Researching the Corruption (1275, from Auberdine), In Search of Thaelrid (1198) and Twilight Falls (1199) (both from Darnassus). Blackfathom Villainy needs 1198 handed in first, so without 1198 you lose it too
[OC]|cffffcc00Supplies:|r there is no vendor inside, so arrive stocked: food and water for an hour, repair, empty bags
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r Forever's Blackfathom is reported to be Classic's dungeon with only the loot changed. Levels, drops, quests and item stats below come from the Forever DB; boss tactics, locations and the brazier event are Classic-era guide knowledge (Icy Veins, Almar's, Forever guides) and not verified on Forever

[OC]|cffffffffBlackfathom Deeps|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, finder level 15 (Classic figure), mobs 22-28, bosses 25-28, ~60 min. Your quests (only Blackfathom Villainy is picked up inside):
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Researching the Corruption (1275) - 8 Corrupted Brain Stems - |cff66ff66normal|r: nine mob types in the DB drop it (every Fallenroot satyr, Blackfathom Tide Priestess, Oracle, Sea Witch, Myrmidon and Lady Sarevess), so the cave mouth and the first caverns usually cover it; the drop rate itself is not in the DB. Hands in to Gershala in Auberdine (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r In Search of Thaelrid (1198) - find Argent Guard Thaelrid in an alcove of Ghamoo-ra's chamber - |cff66ff66normal|r, 2,400 XP on the spot, and he gives Blackfathom Villainy
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Blackfathom Villainy (1200) - the Head of Kelris - |cff66ff66normal|r, a quest drop from Twilight Lord Kelris; 3,300 XP at Selgorm in Darnassus (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Twilight Falls (1199) - 10 Twilight Pendants - |cff66ff66normal|r if you kill every Twilight cultist from the flooded ruins to Kelris (Acolyte, Reaver, Aquamancer, Loreseeker, Shadowmage and Elementalist all drop them; the drop rate is not in the DB, so if you are a few short at the end, go back for the cultists you skipped). 2,550 XP at Manados in Darnassus (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00Maybe:|r The Heart of the Void (78916, level 25): the DB only knows its end, Selgorm in Darnassus, and its text, "Bring the Blackfathom Pearl". Its giver and the Pearl's source are not in the DB (the three reward items are not in the tooltip service yet either). If a Blackfathom Pearl ever drops, keep it and hand it in at Selgorm with the others; this guide does not track the quest
[OC]|cffffcc00Not for you:|r Baron Aquanis, Amongst the Ruins, Allegiance to the Old Gods, The Essence of Aku'mai and Trouble in the Deeps are Horde quests; Alliance has no sapphire quest

|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Gather at the sunken temple on the Zoram Strand and enter Blackfathom Deeps at the cave mouth [G14.5,14.2 Ashenvale]
[OC]|cffffcc00Your job: cat damage|r (Classic reasoning, unverified on Forever): Cat Form, attack what the tank is hitting and stay behind it - Claw to build combo points (Shred from behind), Rip on bosses and Ferocious Bite on trash, Faerie Fire on anything armoured, Tiger's Fury before a burst (Rake, Tiger's Fury and Ferocious Bite only if you trained 24 in Darnassus). Give the tank a few seconds of threat on each pull. If the tank dies, shift to Bear Form and Growl to keep the boss off the healer; Rebirth brings a fallen tank or healer back mid-fight
[OC]|cffffcc00The cave mouth|r is held by elites: Fallenroot Satyrs and Blackfathom Tide Priestesses (level 20-21 in the DB; Forever also lists level-25 versions of both, plus Blackfathom Oracles, in the same spot). Pull them in twos, priestesses (healers) first; each one is already a brain-stem chance
[OC]Classic-era: the way in is a swim through a pool at the foot of the ruins and a winding cave of elite naga; the first cavern inside is crossed on stepping stones over water, and falling in sends you back to the start and usually pulls mobs

[OC]|cffffffffThe run|r  -  one long sweep: Ghamoo-ra's chamber, Lady Sarevess to the north-west, the south tunnel to Gelihast and Lorgus Jett, the water section with Old Serra'kis, the temple and Twilight Lord Kelris, the braziers, Aku'mai. Several trash mobs disarm the tank (Classic-era): ease off for a few seconds after one so you do not pull. Caster naga and murlocs (Sea Witch, Tide Priestess, Oracle) cast and heal: kill them first while the tank pulls them round corners
[OC]|cffffcc00Ghamoo-ra|r (25 elite turtle) in the first big chamber: very high armour, so physical hits do about half damage and the casters do the real work. The tank faces him away from the group; everyone steps out of Trample (random target)
[OC]|cffffcc00Cat (Ghamoo-ra):|r his armour halves Claw and Shred too, so keep Faerie Fire on him and Rip him (a bleed, which ignores armour in Classic); stay behind him and out of Trample
Once the chamber is clear, in the alcove on its south-west side at [TAR4787 Argent Guard Thaelrid], [QT1198] [QA1200 Blackfathom Villainy]
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Ghamoo-ra):|r roll on |cff66ff66Ghamoo-ra's Bind|r (cloth waist +7 Sta, 52.91% drop); |cff66ff66Spiked Shell Band|r (ring +5 Sta, 4.19% drop)
[OC]|cffffcc00Lady Sarevess|r (25 elite naga) with two naga guards in the cavern north-west of the chamber, a short swim away: the tank takes all three, one guard dies first, then the other. Forked Lightning is a frontal cone that chains between targets: nobody stacks or stands in front of her. She also casts Slow and Frost Nova, and she drops Corrupted Brain Stems
[OC]|cffffcc00Cat (Sarevess):|r kill the guard the tank marks first, from behind, then the second; on Sarevess stay at her back so Forked Lightning (frontal cone) never reaches you
Keep looting Corrupted Brain Stems - if you are still short here, they keep dropping from every satyr, priestess, sea witch and myrmidon on the way [QC1275]
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Lady Sarevess):|r roll on |cff66ff66Naga Battle Gloves|r (leather hands +4 Str +4 Sta, 36.62% drop)
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Lorgus Jett):|r roll on |cff66ff66Twilight Maul|r (2H mace 22.9 dps, 14.00% drop)
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Old Serra'kis):|r roll on |cff66ff66Bite of Serra'kis|r (dagger 17.7 dps, 22.66% drop); |cff66ff66Bands of Serra'kis|r (leather wrist +6 Str +3 Sta, 33.41% drop); |cff66ff66Glowing Thresher Cape|r (cloak +8 Spi, 37.86% drop)
[OC]|cffffcc00Gelihast|r (26 elite murloc, skippable for quests, worth it for the loot) at the end of the south tunnel past Ghamoo-ra. The murlocs round him are the real danger: pull one pack at a time, then pull him alone. His Net roots a random player. Click the stone behind him for Blessing of Blackfathom (Classic-era: +5 Int and +5 Spi, a long buff)
[OC]|cffffcc00Lorgus Jett|r (26 elite, optional): a Horde quest target in the northern tunnel after Gelihast (Classic-era: several possible spawns, so skip him if he is not on your path). Lightning Shield hurts melee - you wait for it to drop - and Lightning Bolt on the tank. The Forever DB gives him Twilight Maul, Treacherous Treads and Fallenroot Longbow (one Forever guide lists only the longbow)
[OC]|cffffcc00Baron Aquanis|r (28 elite): summoned by clicking the Fathom Stone in the water section past the fork, and only the Horde quest cares. Leave the stone alone - he drops nothing for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Old Serra'kis|r (26 elite thresher, skippable for quests, worth it for the loot): in the swim-only cave beside the Baron's stone under the ruins. The whole fight is underwater: swim in with Aquatic Form, but you fight in Cat Form with a breath bar, so a Water Breathing potion or a caster's buff first, then burn him fast; he heals himself every so often, so save a burst for it
[OC]|cffffffffThe temple|r  -  above the water the ruins and the temple are full of Twilight cultists (Acolyte, Reaver, Aquamancer, Loreseeker, Shadowmage, Elementalist: level 24-26 elite casters). They are your pendants, so kill every one. Aquamancers are said to summon water elementals (Classic-era): kill the caster first. Pull casters back to the tank and interrupt
Loot Twilight Pendants from the cultists - if you are short, kill the ones you skipped before you start the braziers [QC1199]
[OC]|cffffcc00Twilight Lord Kelris|r (27 elite warlock) in the ceremonial chamber before Aku'mai's door. He pulls the cultists round him into the fight, so clear the room first. Mind Blast hits hard and Sleep takes a player out: a sleeping tank means a second tank or a big threat hit must hold him; dispel the Sleep if you can. Sources disagree on interrupting Mind Blast - try one interrupt and see
[OC]|cffffcc00Cat (Kelris):|r clear the room, let the tank pull him, then Rip and Claw from behind. If Sleep lands on the tank, stop attacking until it breaks; if he turns on the healer, Bear Form and Growl until the tank is back
[OC]|cffffcc00Cat (Aku'mai, after the braziers):|r step out of every Poison Cloud at once (Cure Poison on yourself or the tank if the poison sticks), and ease off during Frenzied Rage so the tank keeps him; Bear Form and Growl if the tank goes down
Kill Twilight Lord Kelris and loot the Head of Kelris [QC1200]
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Twilight Lord Kelris):|r roll on |cff66ff66Rod of the Sleepwalker|r (staff 17.7 dps +11 Spi, 47.99% drop); |cff66ff66Wisdom's Leather Helm|r (leather head +13 Sta); |cff66ff66Gaze Dreamer Pants|r (cloth legs +9 Spi, 32.88% drop)
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Aku'mai):|r roll on |cff66ff66Stormrider's Leather Helm|r (leather head +13 Sta +10 Spi); |cff66ff66Leech Pants|r (cloth legs +5 Sta, 35.17% drop); |cff66ff66Moss Cinch|r (leather waist +5 Sta, 35.80% drop)
[OC]|cffffcc00The braziers|r (Classic-era: four, round the central statue before Aku'mai's door): click one, kill what it calls (Aku'mai Servants, level 26 elite water elementals in the DB), then light the next. The elementals hit in AoE, so kill one as fast as you can and keep the group together. With all four done the door behind the statue opens
[OC]|cffffcc00Aku'mai|r (28 elite hydra) in the lair behind the statue: Poison Cloud on the ground - the tank pulls him out of it and everyone leaves it at once (it can be interrupted); Frenzied Rage (+75% attack speed for about 5 seconds) - stuns and defensive cooldowns then, he can kill a full-health tank quickly
[OC]|cffffcc00Trash loot:|r Doomspike (dagger 17.3 dps, bind on equip, low drop) only if it falls and beats your weapon - roll, never farm; Ring of Precision (+6 Agi +3 Spi, unique) is a cat ring for an empty or weak ring slot; the two caster staves (about 16 dps) are below an 18-dps two-hander, the axes and the Onyx Claymore are not druid weapons and Tree Bark Jacket is cloth - pass

[OC]|cffffcc00After Aku'mai:|r click the stone behind him for Blessing of Blackfathom if you want it. Nothing hands in down here (Thaelrid was the only inside hand-in), and the Hearthstone works from inside the instance, so there is no walk out
|cFFfff8a3Hearth to [H Sentinel Hill]|r
[OC]|cffffffffHand-ins that wait|r  -  1275 Researching the Corruption: Gershala on the Auberdine dock, at chapter 20's Auberdine pass (the boat is not on your way home). 1200 and 1199: Selgorm and Manados in Darnassus, also chapter 20. Keep all of them in the log
[OC]|cffffcc00Training:|r no trainer on this route. If you skipped your level-24 ranks (Rake, Tiger's Fury, Ferocious Bite) in Darnassus, they wait for Sheldras Moontree in the Stormwind Park (chapter 15)
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r log should hold Researching the Corruption (1275), Twilight Falls (1199) and Blackfathom Villainy (1200), all three completed and waiting for hand-ins, plus the carries from chapters 09-12 (1024, 4581, 1035, 1070 and 973 in the plan). Next: walk from Sentinel Hill into Duskwood
[NX 25-26 Duskwood: Darkshire]
]], "Forever Druid 1-30")
